## Publishing

### First time publish

#### Pre-reqs

1. Created an organization in npm registry
2. Have admin access to be able to publish to the organization

#### How-to

Before a package will show up under your organization and allow you to move to the next setup steps for OIDC you will need to publish it once.


1. Navigate to package.json and change the version to be something that you probably wont actually use. For example: `0.0.0-rc`
2. Build and publish the package

```
# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Build the module
pnpm prepack

# Publish the module
pnpm publish --tag rc {% if is_open_source %} --access public{% endif %}

```

3. Navigate to the npm registry console and select the package. Follow details [here](https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers) on how configure OIDC for a Github repo.

> [!NOTE]
> For the CI job to work and publish to npm registry you must setup OIDC..{% endif %}


